</div></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F4.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 4</span>: </span><span id="S3.F4.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
<span id="S3.F4.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">VGGT’s global attention matrix is extremely sparse.</span>
Left: We visualize the tokens corresponding to the top-k activated entries of the attention map of layer 15.
Right: Average &amp; maximum attention scores in the global attention maps; the shorthand {S,P}2{P,S} denotes attention between special (S) and patch (P) tokens.
Layers in the middle of the aggregator exhibit higher activations and increased sparsity.
Note the different scalings of the mean and max activations.
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
